    "# Question: Explain which SQL JOIN type must be used to include restaurants with zero orders and\n",
    "# describe what would happen if an INNER JOIN were used instead. Justify your choice of join type\n",
    "# in terms of how it handles unmatched rows between the two tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Answer: LEFT JOIN vs INNER JOIN\n",
    "\n",
    "We should use a **LEFT JOIN** to include all restaurants, even those with zero orders.\n",
    "\n",
    "A LEFT JOIN returns all rows from the left table (Restaurants) and matching rows from the right table (Orders).\n",
    "\n",
    "If a restaurant has no matching order, the order columns will contain NULL values.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example SQL Query:**\n",
    "\n",
    "```sql\n",
    "SELECT restaurants.restaurant_name,\n",
    "       orders.order_id\n",
    "FROM restaurants\n",
    "LEFT JOIN orders\n",
    "ON restaurants.restaurant_id = orders.restaurant_id;\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### What happens if we use INNER JOIN?\n",
    "\n",
    "INNER JOIN returns only the rows that have matching records in both tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "Restaurants with zero orders will be excluded from the result because they do not have matching records in the Orders table.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "LEFT JOIN is the correct choice because it includes all restaurants, including those with zero orders. INNER JOIN removes unmatched restaurants from the result."
